problem_description:
Perform dimensional analysis for sand-grain roughness parameterization to derive the dimensionless relationship governing the normalized equivalent sand-grain roughness (denoted as ks/Ra).
This analysis uses ONLY the following 7 physical quantities as input parameters:
the first-order absolute moment of height fluctuations, Ra;
the peak-to-valley height, kt;
the root-mean-square height, k_rms;
the skewness of roughness height fluctuations, Sk;
the kurtosis of roughness height fluctuations, Ku;
the effective streamwise slope of the roughness, ES;
the surface porosity, Po.

dimension_detect:
Ra: arithmetic_mean_absolute_height (Ra); First-order absolute moment of surface height fluctuations (mean absolute deviation of height), a measure of average roughness height.; named SI={"M": "0", "L": "1", "T": "0", "I": "0", "Theta": "0", "N": "0", "J": "0"}
kt: peak_to_valley_height (kt); Peak-to-valley height (difference between highest peak and lowest valley) of the surface topography.; named SI={"M": "0", "L": "1", "T": "0", "I": "0", "Theta": "0", "N": "0", "J": "0"}
k_rms: root_mean_square_height (k_rms); Root-mean-square height of surface fluctuations (standard deviation of height), a measure of roughness amplitude.; named SI={"M": "0", "L": "1", "T": "0", "I": "0", "Theta": "0", "N": "0", "J": "0"}
Sk: skewness_of_height_fluctuations (Sk); Skewness of the roughness height distribution (third standardized moment), describes asymmetry of height fluctuations.; named SI={"M": "0", "L": "0", "T": "0", "I": "0", "Theta": "0", "N": "0", "J": "0"}
Ku: kurtosis_of_height_fluctuations (Ku); Kurtosis of the roughness height distribution (fourth standardized moment), describes peakedness/tail weight of height fluctuations.; named SI={"M": "0", "L": "0", "T": "0", "I": "0", "Theta": "0", "N": "0", "J": "0"}
ES: effective_streamwise_slope (ES); Effective streamwise slope of the roughness (dimensionless gradient measure of surface asperities in the flow direction).; named SI={"M": "0", "L": "0", "T": "0", "I": "0", "Theta": "0", "N": "0", "J": "0"}
Po: surface_porosity (Po); Surface porosity (fraction of surface area occupied by voids), a dimensionless fraction between 0 and 1.; named SI={"M": "0", "L": "0", "T": "0", "I": "0", "Theta": "0", "N": "0", "J": "0"}
